Package: fysetc-5inch-dsi
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-current-rockchip64 | linux-headers-edge-rockchip64
Description: Fysetc 5" DSI touchscreen support for BTT Pi2 / CB2 on Armbian
 Display and touch support for the Fysetc 5" MIPI-DSI touchscreen
 (Raspberry Pi 7" touchscreen clone) on the BigTreeTech Pi2 / CB2 (RK3566)
 with mainline Armbian kernels:
  - device-tree overlay enabling the DSI pipeline and I2C2,
  - DKMS build of the raspberrypi-touchscreen panel driver with corrected
    burst mode and panel timing, rebuilt on every kernel update,
  - a polling touch driver for the panel MCU at 0x38 (an FT5406 emulation
   with a non-standard read protocol) that exposes a uinput multitouch device.
 The kernel headers for the running kernel must be installed for DKMS.
